data: name, key/signature/secret key byte sizes\n4. For each of 7 iterations (i=0..6):\n   - Generates 48-byte seed\n   - Computes message length: mlen = 33 * (i + 1)\n   - Generates random message of mlen bytes\n   - Creates keypair: pk (64-128 bytes), sk (128-256 bytes)\n   - Signs message: sm (signature + message)\n   - Verifies: extracts and compares message\n   - Absorbs all values into running transcript hash\n5. Outputs final 32-byte KAT transcript digest in hex\n\n**Hash Backend Selection**:\n- Conditional compilation via BLAKE_TR, HARAKA_TR, SHA2_TR, SHAKE_TR\n- Each backend has identical public interface but different state type/internal functions\n- Transcript absorbs: algorithm name, byte sizes, count, seed, message, keypair, signature\n\n---\n\n### 6. RUST src/main.rs\n\n**Purpose**: Identical KAT generation to C version in pure Rust.\n\n**Key Differences**:\n- Uses Rust's Aes crate for AES (external dependency)\n- Feature flags: \"blake\", \"sha2\", \"shake\", \"haraka\" select hash backend\n- Additional flags: \"128s\", \"128f\", \"192s\", \"192f\", \"256s\", \"256f\" select security level\n- Conditional compilation of KatTrCtx module based on feature flags\n- Uses Vec for dynamic allocations instead of fixed arrays\n- Same transcript structure and 32-byte digest output\n\n**Main Loop**:\n- 7 iterations with BASE_MLEN=33\n- Calls sign::crypto_sign_keypair(), crypto_sign(), crypto_sign_open()\n- Error handling via eprintln! and process::exit()\n- Prints final \"KAT transcript digest = \" followed by 32 hex bytes\n\n---\n\n### SUMMARY\n\nThis is a **SPHINCS+ post-quantum signature scheme implementation** with:\n\n**Dual Implementation**: Full C reference implementation + Rust translation\n**Hash Agility**: Supports BLAKE2/Haraka/SHA-256/SHAKE256 backends (C side-by-side, Rust feature-gated)\n**Security Variants**: 128-bit and 256-bit security levels, fast and small signature sizes\n**Core Algorithm**: Hypertree of Merkle subtrees signed with FORS (Forest of Random Subsets) at base + Winternitz OTS at each layer\n**Testing**: KAT generation program exercising full sign/verify cycle with cryptographic transcript verification"}],"totalDurationMs":94347,"totalTokens":87540,"totalToolUseCount":57,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6169,"cache_read_input_tokens":76092,"output_tokens":5272,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6169},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
