{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AfzXZKWRVEnHcvdbKqycUi","type":"tool_result","content":"300\tvoid blake256_update( blakestate256 *S, const u8 *data, u64 datalen ) {\n301\t\n302\t  int left=S->buflen >> 3; \n303\t  int fill=64 - left;\n304\t   \n305\t  if( left && ( ((datalen >> 3) & 0x3F) >= fill ) ) {\n306\t    memcpy( (void*) (S->buf + left), (void*) data, fill );\n307\t    S->t[0] += 512;\n308\t    if (S->t[0] == 0) S->t[1]++;      \n309\t    blake256_compress( S, S->buf );\n310\t    data += fill;\n311\t    datalen  -= (fill << 3);       \n312\t    left = 0;\n313\t  }\n314\t\n315\t  while( datalen >= 512 ) {\n316\t    S->t[0] += 512;\n317\t    if (S->t[0] == 0) S->t[1]++;\n318\t    blake256_compress( S, data );\n319\t    data += 64;\n320\t    datalen -= 512;\n321\t  }\n322\t  \n323\t  if( datalen > 0 ) {\n324\t    memcpy( (void*) (S->buf + left), (void*) data, datalen>>3 );\n325\t    S->buflen = (left<<3) + datalen;\n326\t  }\n327\t  else S->buflen=0;\n328\t}\n329\t\n330\t\n331\tvoid blake256_final( blakestate256 *S, u8 *digest ) {\n332\t  \n333\t  u8 msglen[8], zo=0x01, oo=0x81;\n334\t  u32 lo=S->t[0] + S->buflen, hi=S->t[1];\n335\t  if ( lo < S->buflen ) hi++;\n336\t  U32TO8(  msglen + 0, hi );\n337\t  U32TO8(  msglen + 4, lo );\n338\t\n339\t  if ( S->buflen == 440 ) { /* one padding byte */\n340\t    S->t[0] -= 8;\n341\t    blake256_update( S, &oo, 8 );\n342\t  }\n343\t  else {\n344\t    if ( S->buflen < 440 ) { /* enough space to fill the block  */\n345\t      if ( !S->buflen ) S->nullt=1;\n346\t      S->t[0] -= 440 - S->buflen;\n347\t      blake256_update( S, padding, 440 - S->buflen );\n348\t    }\n349\t    else { /* need 2 compressions */\n350\t      S->t[0] -= 512 - S->buflen; \n351\t      blake256_update( S, padding, 512 - S->buflen );\n352\t      S->t[0] -= 440;\n353\t      blake256_update( S, padding+1, 440 );\n354\t      S->nullt = 1;\n355\t    }\n356\t    blake256_update( S, &zo, 8 );\n357\t    S->t[0] -= 8;\n358\t  }\n359\t  S->t[0] -= 64;"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"40cff8f1-55c4-4312-944f-3a5007119e9f","uuid":"61ffe0dc-663d-469b-bc37-cbb3d795649a","timestamp":"2026-04-02T12:25:48.289Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/harvest-verify-A83WWg/translated_rust/c_src/lib/blake/src/blake256.c","content":"void blake256_update( blakestate256 *S, const u8 *data, u64 datalen ) {\n\n  int left=S->buflen >> 3; \n  int fill=64 - left;\n   \n  if( left && ( ((datalen >> 3) & 0x3F) >= fill ) ) {\n    memcpy( (void*) (S->buf + left), (void*) data, fill );\n    S->t[0] += 512;\n    if (S->t[0] == 0) S->t[1]++;      \n    blake256_compress( S, S->buf );\n    data += fill;\n    datalen  -= (fill << 3);       \n    left = 0;\n  }\n\n  while( datalen >= 512 ) {\n    S->t[0] += 512;\n    if (S->t[0] == 0) S->t[1]++;\n    blake256_compress( S, data );\n    data += 64;\n    datalen -= 512;\n  }\n  \n  if( datalen > 0 ) {\n    memcpy( (void*) (S->buf + left), (void*) data, datalen>>3 );\n    S->buflen = (left<<3) + datalen;\n  }\n  else S->buflen=0;\n}\n\n\nvoid blake256_final( blakestate256 *S, u8 *digest ) {\n  \n  u8 msglen[8], zo=0x01, oo=0x81;\n  u32 lo=S->t[0] + S->buflen, hi=S->t[1];\n  if ( lo < S->buflen ) hi++;\n  U32TO8(  msglen + 0, hi );\n  U32TO8(  msglen + 4, lo );\n\n  if ( S->buflen == 440 ) { /* one padding byte */\n    S->t[0] -= 8;\n    blake256_update( S, &oo, 8 );\n  }\n  else {\n    if ( S->buflen < 440 ) { /* enough space to fill the block  */\n      if ( !S->buflen ) S->nullt=1;\n      S->t[0] -= 440 - S->buflen;\n      blake256_update( S, padding, 440 - S->buflen );\n    }\n    else { /* need 2 compressions */\n      S->t[0] -= 512 - S->buflen; \n      blake256_update( S, padding, 512 - S->buflen );\n      S->t[0] -= 440;\n      blake256_update( S, padding+1, 440 );\n      S->nullt = 1;\n    }\n    blake256_update( S, &zo, 8 );\n    S->t[0] -= 8;\n  }\n  S->t[0] -= 64;","numLines":60,"startLine":300,"totalLines":403}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016FoELjFEkQfnNSiDpDDNhb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I see a critical difference! In C's `blake256_update` line 305:\n```c\nif( left && ( ((datalen >> 3) & 0x3F) >= fill ) )\n```\n\nIt has `& 0x3F` masking! The Rust code doesn't have this mask:\n```rust\nif left != 0 && (datalen_remaining >> 3) as i32 >= fill {\n```\n\nAlso, in C's `blake256_update`, line 327: `else S->buflen=0;` - when `datalen == 0` and there was no leftover data, it sets buflen to 0. But in Rust, the else branch sets `s.buflen = (left << 3) as i32` which preserves the left value. Wait, looking more carefully:\n\nIn C line 327: `else S->buflen=0;` This is unconditional - when `datalen <= 0`, set buflen to 0.\n\nIn Rust line 239-241:\n```rust\n} else {\n    s.buflen = (left << 3) as i32;\n}\n```\nThis preserves `left` instead of setting to 0. That's wrong! The C code sets `buflen=0` when `datalen == 0` regardless of `left`.\n\nWait, actually looking at the C code more carefully at line 323-328:\n```c\nif( datalen > 0 ) {\n    memcpy( (void*) (S->buf + left), (void*) data, datalen>>3 );\n    S->buflen = (left<<3) + datalen;\n}\nelse S->buflen=0;\n```\n\nSo when datalen is 0 (no remaining data), C sets buflen to 0. But the Rust code sets `s.buflen = (left << 3) as i32` which is wrong - it should be `s.buflen = left << 3` only if... wait no, let me re-read the C. The C says `else S->buflen=0`. That means if no data remains after the loop, the buffer length is 0. But the Rust preserves `left`.\n\nActually wait - if we got past the first `if` and the `while` loop, and `left` was set to 0 by the first if block, then `left << 3` is also 0. So they'd match in that case. But if the first `if` block wasn't entered (because `left` was 0 initially or datalen was too small), and then `datalen` became 0 after the while loop...\n\nActually let me think more carefully. If `left != 0` and the first if fires, `left` becomes 0. Then after the while loop, if `datalen_remaining == 0`, C sets buflen to 0, Rust sets `buflen = 0 << 3 = 0`. Same.\n\nIf `left != 0` but the first if doesn't fire (datalen too small), we skip it. Then datalen might still be > 0 after the while loop (or might not enter the while). If datalen becomes exactly 0 after while, then C sets buflen=0 but Rust sets buflen = `left << 3` where `left` is still nonzero. This is a bug!\n\nAlso there's the `& 0x3F` issue in the first condition. Let me fix both issues."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1105,"cache_read_input_tokens":89803,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1105},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"40cff8f1-55c4-4312-944f-3a5007119e9f","uuid":"aff223dd-7271-4cc2-8a26-90b6a30bc29a"}
