non-absorbed bytes count)\n\n**Process:**\n1. Loop while `(mlen + s_inc[64]) >= HARAKAS_RATE` (HARAKAS_RATE = 32 bytes):\n   - XOR `(HARAKAS_RATE - s_inc[64])` bytes from message into state starting at offset `s_inc[64]`\n   - Decrement `mlen` by bytes consumed\n   - Advance message pointer\n   - Reset `s_inc[64] = 0`\n   - Apply `haraka512_perm()` to full state\n2. After loop, XOR remaining `mlen` bytes into state at offset `s_inc[64]`\n3. Increment `s_inc[64]` by `mlen`\n\n**Key Point:** The function handles partial blocks by tracking position in byte 64.\n\n---\n\n### 3. **haraka_S_inc_finalize Function**\n\n**File:** `/tmp/harvest-verify-A83WWg/translated_rust/c_src/lib/haraka/src/haraka.c` (lines 794-801)\n\n```c\nvoid haraka_S_inc_finalize(uint8_t *s_inc)\n```\n\n**Exact Logic:**\n1. XOR `0x1F` (domain separator) at position `s_inc[64]` in state\n2. XOR `0x80` (padding byte) at position 31 (HARAKAS_RATE - 1)\n3. Reset `s_inc[64] = 0`\n\n**Purpose:** Finalizes the sponge after absorption, adding domain separation and padding.\n\n---\n\n### 4. **haraka_S_inc_squeeze Function**\n\n**File:** `/tmp/harvest-verify-A83WWg/translated_rust/c_src/lib/haraka/src/haraka.c` (lines 803-829)\n\n**Exact Logic:**\n1. **First phase - consume cached bytes:**\n   - Loop while `(i < outlen) && (i < s_inc[64])`:\n     - Copy bytes from position `(HARAKAS_RATE - s_inc[64] + i)` in state\n     - Advance `out` and decrement `outlen`\n     - Decrement `s_inc[64]`\n\n2. **Second phase - generate new blocks:**\n   - While `outlen > 0`:\n     - Apply `haraka512_perm()` to state\n     - Copy min(`outlen`, `HARAKAS_RATE`) bytes from state start\n     - Update `s_inc[64]` to track remaining bytes in current block\n\n**Key Detail:** Maintains cached bytes for partial block extraction via `s_inc[64]` tracking.\n\n---\n\n### 5. **tweak_constants Function**\n\n**File:** `/tmp/harvest-verify-A83WWg/translated_rust/c_src/lib/haraka/src/haraka.c` (lines 701-715)\n\n```c\nvoid tweak_constants(spx_ctx *ctx)\n```\n\n**Exact Logic:**\n1. Copy 640 bytes (40 x 16 bytes = 10 rounds x 8 words x 8 bytes) from static `haraka512_rc64` to `ctx->tweaked512_rc64`\n2. Generate 640 bytes of random material: `haraka_S(buf, 640, ctx->pub_seed, SPX_N, ctx)`\n3. Loop for 10 rounds (i = 0 to 9):\n   - Interleave 32 bytes of buf into 32-bit tweaked constants: `interleave_constant32(ctx->tweaked256_rc32[i], buf + 32*i)`\n   - Interleave 64 bytes of buf into 64-bit tweaked constants: `interleave_constant(ctx->tweaked512_rc64[i], buf + 64*i)`\n\n**Data Sizes:**\n- Round constants: 10 rounds × 2 sub-rounds = 20 total round key applications\n- Each tweaked constant set: 8 x 64-bit words (512 bits) for 512-bit variant, 8 x 32-bit words for 256-bit variant\n\n---\n\n### 6. **haraka512 Function (Non-Perm)**\n\n**File:** `/tmp/harvest-verify-A83WWg/translated_rust/c_src/lib/haraka/src/haraka.c` (lines 902-919)\n\n```c\nvoid haraka512(unsigned char *out, const unsigned char *in, const spx_ctx *ctx)\n```\n\n**Exact Logic:**\n1. Create 64-byte temporary buffer\n2. Call `haraka512_perm(buf, in, ctx)` to get permuted output\n3. **Feed-forward:** XOR all 64 bytes of permutation output with original input\n4. **Truncation** - copy 32 bytes to output in specific pattern:\n   - `out[0-7]` = `buf[8-15]`\n   - `out[8-15]` = `buf[24-31]`\n   - `out[16-23]` = `buf[32-39]`\n   - `out[24-31]` = `buf[48-55]`\n\n**Output:** 32 bytes (4 x 8-byte chunks from non-contiguous positions)\n\n---\n\n### 7. **haraka256 Function**\n\n**File:** `/tmp/harvest-verify-A83WWg/translated_rust/c_src/lib/haraka/src/haraka.c` (lines 922-965)\n\n```c\nvoid haraka256(unsigned char *out, const unsigned char *in,\n        const spx_ctx *ctx)\n```\n\n**Exact Logic:**\n1. Load 32-byte input into 8 x 32-bit state values using 32-bit little-endian decoding:\n   - `q[2*i] = br_dec32le(in + 4*i)` for i=0..3\n   - `q[2*i+1] = br_dec32le(in + 4*i + 16)` for i=0..3\n2. Apply orthogonal transformation: `br_aes_ct_ortho(q)`\n3. Execute 5 r