{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01A8mapu3Dwjfavb44kv2KGc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's a summary of all the bugs found and fixed:\n\n## Summary of Bugs Fixed\n\n### BLAKE implementation (`blake_impl.rs`)\n1. **Missing `BlakeState256::new()` and `BlakeState512::new()`** - Added constructor methods\n2. **`blake256_update` missing `& 0x3F` mask** in the fill condition - Added `& 0x3F` to match C\n3. **`blake256_update` incorrect else branch** - Set `buflen = 0` instead of preserving `left`, matching C's `else S->buflen=0`\n4. **`blake256_update` wrong buflen formula** - Use `(left << 3) + datalen` to match C's `(left<<3) + datalen`\n5. **`blake512_update` same three issues** - Applied `& 0x7F` mask, `buflen = 0` in else, and correct buflen formula\n6. **`blake512_final` wrong padding constant** - Changed from `896` to `888` (matching C)\n7. **`blake256_final` missing overflow increment** - Added `hi += 1` when `lo < buflen`\n8. **`blake512_final` same overflow issue** - Added `hi += 1`\n\n### BLAKE hash functions (`hash.rs`)\n9. **`gen_message_random` passed `SPX_N * 8` instead of `SPX_N` to blake_update** - C passes byte counts (not bit counts) to `blake*_update`, Rust must match\n10. **`hash_message` same issue** - Fixed `R`, `pk`, and `m` length arguments\n11. **`gen_message_random` wrote 32/64 bytes to SPX_N-sized output** - Added temp buffer for blake256/512_final output\n\n### BLAKE KAT transcript (`main.rs`)\n12. **All `blake*_update` calls multiplied by 8** - Removed `* 8` multipliers to match C's byte-based calling convention\n\n### SHA-256/SHA-512 (`sha2_impl.rs`)\n13. **`crypto_hashblocks_sha256` wrong message schedule** - Inline w[] update during each round was wrong; refactored to batch EXPAND + 16 rounds (matching C's EXPAND_32 macro pattern)\n14. **`crypto_hashblocks_sha512` same issue** - Applied same batch expansion fix\n\n### SHA-2 hash (`hash.rs`)\n15. **Borrow checker error in `gen_message_random`** - Fixed by cloning input slice before passing to `sha256_inc_finalize`\n\n### SHAKE/Keccak (`fips202.rs`)\n16. **`keccak_inc_finalize` called `KeccakF1600_StatePermute` but C does not** - Removed the permutation call (C defers permutation to squeeze phase)\n\n### Haraka (`haraka_impl.rs`)\n17. **Wrong round constants** - Rows 2-9 of `haraka512_rc64` were incorrect; replaced with values from C source\n18. **`br_aes_ct64_interleave_in` used full bit-level interleave instead of byte-level** - Removed 3 extra spreading steps and changed final combine from `<< 1` to `<< 8`\n19. **`br_aes_ct64_interleave_out` used full bit-level de-interleave** - Fixed to use byte-level de-interleave matching C\n20. **`haraka_S_inc_squeeze` did extra unnecessary permutation** - Rewrote to match C's `while (outlen > 0) { permute; output; }` pattern\n\n### Exports (`lib.rs`)\n21. **Created `lib.rs` with `#[no_mangle] pub extern \"C\"` wrappers** for all C-exported symbols across all 4 backends (blake, sha2, shake, haraka)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":313,"cache_read_input_tokens":244669,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":313},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"40cff8f1-55c4-4312-944f-3a5007119e9f","uuid":"58f50e62-6d53-4abb-aff3-bb541141a7e0"}
